        "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$",
        "worked_solution": "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{3}(2{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{x}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
